Zhalia Moon received Gareon as her first [[Titan]] after being adopted by [[the Organization|the Organization's]] scientist, [[Klaus]]. {{source|The Vampire Loses Its Fangs}} Training for years alongside her Titan, they developed a bond much tighter than most [[Seekers]] ever have with their Titans. {{source|Huntik.com}} Her Gareon even behaved like a pet cat when she was feeling down.

Gareon helped to defeat a [[Redcap]] in the [[Prague Huntik Hotel]], when Zhalia came to the rescue of [[Dante Vale]], [[Lok Lambert]] and [[Sophie Casterwill]] from some [[Suits]]. Gareon was later invoked by Zhalia alongside [[Kilthane]] in the attic of [[Jodis Lore]]. After turning invisible, Gareon snuck behind Grier and stunned him with his eye beams. {{source|Words of Truth, Heart of Lies}}

Zhalia invoked Gareon whilst rescuing [[Peter]] from a pair of police officers in Paris. Turning invisible, Gareon was able to stun the policemen while Zhalia and Peter made their mistake. Gareon was later invoked to fight in the [[Cave of the Gargoyle]] against the Organization forces. {{source|Into the River of Secrets}}

Gareon played a vital role in getting the [[Ring of Arc]] to [[Clements]] at the [[Cathedral of Notre Dame]], using his invisibility to sneak past the Organization forces spread throughout the [[Paris Catacombs]]. He was later seen being held by Zhalia at the safehouse following the team's mission. {{source|Divide and Conquer}}

In Iceland, Zhalia and Gareon attempted to slow [[Ymir]] down by blasting him in the face. {{source|The Legacy of Thor}} Gareon was later used in the [[Temple of Thor]] to hold back the [[Guardians of Thor]]. {{source|Two Powers Become One}}

Zhalia used Gareon in the [[Basilisk House]] where he surprised Lok and Sophie. His Amulet was later taken by [[DeFoe]] and left in a bag when Zhalia, Sophie and Lok were ambushed and taken prisoner. After Zhalia freed herself, Gareon took Defoe's bag and gave it to Lok and Sophie, enabling them to invoke [[Freelancer]] and [[Sabriel]] against the Organization. {{source|Absent Heroes}}

Gareon was used when Zhalia fought against [[Grier]] in the hull of the shipwreck, but was defeated by his [[Dragonfist]] power. {{source|The Treasures of the Argonauts}} On [[Madea Island]], an illusion of Gareon was invoked against Zhalia alongside [[Kilthane]] and [[Strix]] by an image of a young Zhalia, created by the Titan [[Madea]]. Garion attacked Lok's [[Freelancer]] but was defeated. {{source|The Beautiful Trap}}

Gareon was used to attack one [[Klaus|Klaus's]] men in the [[Tomb of Nefertiti]] while the Huntik team tried to escape with the [[Sceptre of Nefertiti]]. {{source|The Sceptre Deception}} Gareon was later used to attack Sophie in the [[Castle of Vlad Dracul]] after Zhalia betrayed the team to Klaus. His attacks were blocked by Sophie's [[Honorguard]]. {{source|The Vampire Loses Its Fangs}}

Gareon was seen comforting Zhalia in her [[Zhalia Moon's apartment|apartment]] as she pondered over how she could make up for betraying Dante and his team. {{source|Ladies' Choice}}

Gareon was used to attack two of [[Rassimov|Rassimov's]] Suits in [[King Solomon's Mines]]. After stunning one Suit, he was hit by an [[Augerfrost]] before running away. {{source|To Be Together}}

Zhalia invoked Gareon to fight against Sophie in [[The Professor's castle]] when the two came into conflict over Dante's decision to give [[the Professor]] the [[Rings]] of [[Behemoth]] and [[Tao]]. After defeating [[Icarus]], Gareon was sent back to his Amulet by Sabriel. {{source|The Divine Comedy}} Gareon later fought alongside [[Hoplite]] against two [[Undergolem]] Titans summoned by [[Eathon the dog]] but both were defeated. {{source|The Mission}}

Following the defeat of the Professor, Gareon was used to take out two Suits during the team's attack on [[Organization Central]]. Gareon was later used in [[Peru]] to defeat a [[Mindrone]] summoned by the forces of [[Wilder]].{{source|Doorway to Huntik}}

Zhalia summoned Gareon in the [[Crystal Caves]] where he fought alongside Dante's [[Caliban]] and Lok's [[Lindorm]] against [[White|White's]] [[Palamedes]] and [[Mallory|Mallory's]] [[Pellinore]]. After a fierce battle, Gareon was defeated by Palamedes. {{source|Cave of the Casterwills}}

On the island of [[Medusa]], Gareon assisted Zhalia in tracking down [[Stack]] and the [[Blood Spiral]] Seeker [[Kiel]]. Zhalia pondered to Gareon over infiltrating the cave before leaving while Gareon returned to his Amulet. {{source|Zhalia's Mission}}

When Zhalia was caught infiltrating the [[Blood Spiral]] by [[Tantras]], Gareon [[Powerbonded]] with her. Using his Scramblemind ability, the two erased Tantras' memory of her being a double-agent. {{source|Sophie on Trial}}

Powerbonded Gareon again was invoked during the confrontation against [[the Betrayer]] and [[Demigorgan]] when Zhalia rejoined her team. Using his Camouflage ability, Gareon managed to sneak through the battle and land a direct attack to Demigorgan. However, Demigorgan used its abilities to summon a copy of Zhalia to confuse and subvert the Rapport-Bond. The copy of Zhalia then transformed itself into the Titan before it was defeated by [[Pendragon|Powerbonded Pendragon]]. Gareon rejoined Zhalia and the others and later assisted [[Lucas Casterwill]] and [[Sandra Lambert]] in their attack on the Betrayer. However, after dodging multiple attacks, Gareon was defeated by the Betrayer's ability to use the Spiral Mark to revive himself. {{source|Dante's Return}}

[[File:S2E39 Tantras Gareon Zhalia Scramblemind.png|thumb|Zhalia tries to erase [[Tantras]]' memories with Powerbonded Gareon's '''Scramblemind'''|199x199px]]
After forming a tight bond with his Seeker, Gareon grew significantly in size and became equipped with armor covering his chest and a reptilian frill around his head. His eyes too changed from yellow to red. {{Source|Sophie on Trial}} His speed and maneuverability has increased, and his eye blasts are now significantly more powerful. {{source|Dante's Return}} His new Powerbonded abilities include:
*'''Camouflage''' - renders him invisible, far more potent than his previous Limited Invisibility power. {{source|Dante's Return}}
*'''Scramblemind''' - allows him and Zhalia to manipulate opponents' minds and erase their short-term memories. {{source|Sophie on Trial}}

